hat there's a  demon in the area but it's really just a  Caza Mouzon goes on to turn akasa into a  demon and he loses his memories he wants  strength once again even though there's  nothing  left for him to protect he didn't want  to live anymore but moves on turned him  into a demon who would go on to murder  people pointlessly for over a hundred  years so that's the back story of a casa  interestingly enough even though he lost  his memories he was the only demon who  refused to kill or eat women even as a  brainwashed demon he still continued to  hold on to some principles that he  wouldn't break now let's go back to the  fight it was heading towards a  conclusion but koi Yuki's ghost helps  our Casas realize that there is no  longer a reason for him to keep fighting  his goal was to get stronger so he could  protect his loved ones but his loved  ones are long dead and he would have  been dead by now too if he didn't turn  into a demon thus he has no more reasons  to fight he has no more reasons to get  stronger ton zero wakes up and starts  rushing towards a casa but has no  strength in his hand so he drops the  sword it seems like it's over but Akasa  realizes that this whole time when he  was killing others he was actually  trying to kill himself  he smiles at Angira then he self  destructs in a way where he wouldn't  hurt the demon hunters he decides to go  to hell gracefully and in between this  world and the next he sees his father  son say and lover again he apologizes  for what he became but they all still  love him they haven't forsaken him even  if they can't take him to heaven koyuki  once again gives him permission to let  go Naza cries in her arms and she  welcomes her love home he himself says  his home before he and koyuki are  consumed by the flames of hell what a  field trip I can't remember the last  time a character story affected me as  much as a cos øz did he truly is a  product of an unfair world yet even in  an unfair world he never fully let go of  his humanity and in the end he turned  back into his old self he tried to save  his father's life and he was punished  for it then his dad killed himself  then after hitting rock bottom he  decided to give life on the other chance  he completely dedicated himself to  helping kaizo and koyuki things started  looking good he started to really  believe that he could live a good life  and for the second time it was all  snatched away from him  he took revenge on the people who  snatched it all from him and then moves  on found him  he no longer cared about anything he  brainwashed him and turned him into a  demon yet even though he lost his  memories he still refused to eat or kill  women he still held on to some moral  principles he was so strong that he  couldn't even be beaten by our main  characters he had to choose to die he  died on his own terms while he could  have potentially went on and killed GU  Anton judo yes he killed rain Goku  but the whole time he was hoping not to  kill him he was trying to turn him into  a demon and at the time Octus I didn't  think that was a bad thing in the end he  was an accidental villain he was turned  into a villain by the circumstances of  his life by the cruel world and when he  regained his memories he defeated  himself and gracefully went to hell if  he wasn't forced to become a criminal to  save his father  and if his loved ones weren't poisoned  he would have lived the right kind of  life like his father wanted him to for  all these reasons I amplified with a  kazoo he did horrible things especially  as a demon so he has to atone for those  sins however you can see how he got  there the manga shows us how even a  selfless caring person can become a  monster under the right or should I say  wrong conditions and it's completely  believable I think our cuz those loved  ones were right not to forsake him yes  he made big mistakes but Icaza isn't a  bad guy at heart  in fact his whole story illustrates how  even good people can be made to do  really bad things this is why fiction  like demon slayer is important it makes  us more empathetic it helps us realize  that we don't always know what people  are going through we can't judge a book  by its cover and we shouldn't assume  that someone's a terrible person because  they have pickpocketing tattoos and as  we become more empathetic we realize  that we all have to do our part to make  this world a better place so that there  will be less cruelty in the world and in  turn less monsters born from that  cruelty and that is it for today's video  thank you so much for watching let me  know who your absolute favorite villain  and anime is and why in the comments if  you enjoyed this video make sure to  smash that like button to let me know if  you haven't be sure to subscribe and  ring that notification bell so you  actually get notified when new videos  drop for more content including crucial  anime updates follow us on Instagram and  at Anime uproar a big thank you goes out  to our patrons on patreon who help make  videos like this one possible I  especially want to thank our pro hero to  your patrons the one and only Gilgamesh  nothing but a fan Jason Wilson Kings  August angel Cruz Steelers and Pablo  Pablo and are the one tier patrons the  ones who stay atop all clans baby ray a  seventeen ffvp Steven Ingrid ah a Lola  autumn Mattie Mac 239 makoto-kun keelon  and elrico dames and the Patriots who  transcend greatness itself Regan  Harrison and Lord Noxon or the chosen  few who have been acknowledged by Lord  we go himself if you enjoy our work you  can support more of it by going over to  patreon calm animals roar and becoming a  patron today for as little as $1 if you  do so you'll get your name featured in  future videos alongside these amazing  people right here and you'll even get  access to our private patient only  discord  so check out patreon.com/lenguin  if you're interested and until next time  see you space cowboy  [Mu